{
  "_doc": "What a correct ingestion looks like, per source, checked on every build. `coverage` is a recorded baseline with a tolerance — it catches a truncated download or a partial extract, the failure that otherwise looks like a smaller dataset. `golden` records are specific facts that must survive every build. A golden record is either VERIFIED (checked against the publisher by a human, with the date and method) or a BASELINE (captured from a verified build, and so evidence of stability only, never of truth). The distinction is enforced, not conventional: a regression test presented as a fact-check is the same move as stamping hand-written prose with an upstream's citation.",
